     "id": "export_flux_average_solid",
     "description": "The solid-runoff average law, from the SOURCE FORMULA (glad_output_fluxes.F90:104-105, 143-161; the dump carries only zeros): over one coupling interval [0, T_coupling] with constant calving_rate = 1.5 m/yr = 1.5/3.1536e7 m/s and removal_rate = 0.25 m/yr, D(S_rofi)/dt = rhoi*(calving_rate + removal_rate) integrates to S_rofi(T) = rhoi*1.75/3.1536e7 * T = rhoi*1.75 m (1.75 m of ice lost per year), and rofi = S_rofi/T_coupling = 917*1.75/3.1536e7 = 5.088628868594622e-05 kg/m2/s. The Fortran's per-step sum with piecewise-constant rates gives the identical value (sum_k rhoi*(m_k)/dt / count = rhoi*sum(m_k)/T). The intermediate assertion at t = T/2 pins the accumulation itself (S_rofi = rhoi*1.75/2 = 802.375 kg/m2), not just the end state.",
